<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ana Sagar Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Anasagar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ana Sagar is an artificial lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in the mid-12th century by the Chahamana king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnoraja">Arnoraja</a>, also called Anaji, after whom it is named, by damming a stream in the Aravalli hills. The Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a> laid out the Daulat Bagh gardens beside it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> added marble pavilions on its embankment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ana-sagar-lake.jpg" alt="Ana Sagar Lake" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fatehrawkey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Anas%C4%81gar_Lake_1_PHOTOGRAPHED_BY_FATEH.RawKEy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Setting</h2><p>Ana Sagar is the largest lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> and has the city's largest catchment, of which about 5 square kilometres is built up. It spreads over 13 km, reaches a maximum depth of 4.4 m and holds about 4,750,000 cubic metres of water. An island in the middle can be reached by boat from the east side of the Daulat Bagh, and the lakeside walkways known as the Chowpatty and the Jetty run beside the Baradari. A circuit house on a nearby hill was once Lodha's Residency.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnoraja">Arnoraja</a>, also called Ana, came to the throne a little before 1133 and was the grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a>. Early in his reign he crushed an army of Turuskas that had advanced as far as Pushkar, worn out by their long march through the desert; a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> prashasti says the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> was soaked with their blood. On the plain where the battle was fought he built the lake, with the help of the local people, and filled it from the river Chandra, which the historian H. C. Ray identified with the Luni and Sarda with the Bandi.</p><p>The Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a> laid out the Daulat Bagh garden beside the lake, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> built five pavilions, the Baradari, between the garden and the water. From 2023 the National Green Tribunal and then the Supreme Court heard petitions by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a> activist Ashok Malik against structures raised in the lake's wetland buffer under Ajmer Smart City projects. On 18 March 2025 the Supreme Court ordered the removal of encroachments in the Seven Wonders Park and of a food court at Luv-Kush Garden, and that year demolition of the replicas began.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">The place today</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan-high-court">Rajasthan High Court</a> has banned building in the catchment areas of the lake. On its bank lies Rishi Udyan, where the ashes of Dayananda Saraswati, who died near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a>, were scattered as he had wished. It holds an Arya Samaj temple and an annual gathering on the anniversary of his death, organised by the Paropkarini Sabha, which he founded in 1880 and which has worked from Ajmer since 1893.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Ana Sagar Lake” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Ajayaraja founded Ajmer around 1113 and made it the capital, and Arnoraja built the <b>Ana Sagar</b> lake.</blockquote><a href="/state/chahamanas-of-shakambhari">Chahamanas of Shakambhari</a></li></ul></section>
